{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_013QVxtP32Jhj4EXbJ6nHRcA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/02-017-what-is-hybrid-search-when-combine-vector-bm25.md`** for Q17: *What is hybrid search? When combine vector + BM25?*\n\nKey content:\n- **Concept:** Sparse (BM25 inverted index) + dense (bi-encoder HNSW) cover complementary failure modes — dense misses exact keywords/SKUs, sparse misses paraphrase\n- **Mechanism:** Two parallel retrieval legs → merged via **Reciprocal Rank Fusion** (`score = Σ 1/(k + rank)`, k=60) — rank-based so no score normalization needed → optional cross-encoder reranker (Cohere Rerank, `bge-reranker-large`) for top-K\n- **Concrete stack:** Elasticsearch 8.9+ native hybrid+RRF, Qdrant sparse+dense fields, LangChain `EnsembleRetriever`\n- **Production example:** SKU dense-only failure → hybrid fixed (Recall@5 61%→79%, NDCG@5 0.58→0.74)\n- **Pitfalls:** Averaging raw scores (wrong — use ranks), not naming the failure mode, forgetting both indexes need synchronized CDC updates\n\nNext up: Q18 — *What is re-ranking? Cross-encoder vs bi-encoder?*"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":59523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":369,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e82ce3f3-76d3-4120-ad67-2ecc448398e4","uuid":"dbe5dd4d-fcee-4d86-bf21-b4f8448d7d97"}
